   "title": "ChatGPT can lock your chats now, but it is not encryption",
   "tiktok_caption": "ChatGPT can now lock private chats behind a four digit code, but OpenAI says it is not encryption. Reset the code and locked chats are deleted. #ChatGPT #AI #Privacy #OpenAI #TechTips #FredsDesk #fyp",
   "yt_caption": "ChatGPT's new Locked Chats hides chats from history and search behind a four digit code, or your face or fingerprint on supported phones. Locked chats get their own memory. But OpenAI says it is not end-to-end encryption and does not change data retention. Resetting the code deletes everything locked. Follow FredsDesk for daily AI",
   "pinned_comment": "Locked Chats is rolling out gradually, so it may not be on your account yet. It hides chats from people looking at your screen or device; per OpenAI it is not end-to-end encryption, does not change how long OpenAI keeps chats and does not change your 'Improve the model for everyone' setting. Anything ChatGPT remembered before you locked a chat stays in regular memory. Sources: OpenAI Help Center, Beebom, WinCentral, AI Weekly.",
